        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued July 15 at 1:27PM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
        "description": "A glacier dammed lake outburst from Summit Lake continues on the\nSalmon River near Hyder. Water levels on the Salmon River are\nexpected to continue to rise over the next day or two with an\nexpected crest sometime later today or Thursday. It is unknown how\nmuch water will be released from Summit Lake which results in large\nuncertainty on crest height and timing.\n\nPotential impact area for this event is the road from Hyder to\nPremier, Canada at around mile point 9 along the Salmon River.\n\nBe aware",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Observed",
